      "page_title": "Restart & Recovery Behaviour",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Load Precedence",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Redis boots",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
                "b0",
                "b1"
              ],
              [
                "c0_0",
                "c0_1"
              ],
              [
                "c1_0"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "n0": {
                "text": "Redis boots",
                "shape": "diamond"
              },
              "b0": {
                "text": "`appendonly yes`",
                "shape": "box"
              },
              "b1": {
                "text": "`appendonly no`",
                "shape": "box"
              },
              "c0_0": {
                "text": "loads AOF",
                "shape": "box"
              },
              "c0_1": {
                "text": "ignores dump.rdb",
                "shape": "box"
              },
              "c1_0": {
                "text": "loads dump.rdb",
                "shape": "box"
              }
            },
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b0"
              },
              {
                "from": "n0",
                "to": "b1"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_0"
              },
              {
                "from": "b0",
                "to": "c0_1"
              },
              {
                "from": "b1",
                "to": "c1_0"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "AOF wins because it is the more complete record",
            "There is no merge — the RDB is simply not read"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The #1 Loss Trap",
          "text": "Good RDB on disk, you add `appendonly yes` to the config and restart: Redis reads an empty AOF and boots an empty dataset."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# safe enablement, at runtime, RDB already loaded",
            "redis-cli CONFIG SET appendonly yes",
            "redis-cli INFO persistence | grep rewrite",
            "redis-cli CONFIG REWRITE   # persist to the file"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "While It Loads"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`INFO persistence` reports `loading:1`",
            "Clients get `-LOADING Redis is loading the dataset in memory`",
            "Progress: `loading_total_bytes`, `loading_loaded_perc`",
            "Plus `loading_eta_seconds`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "RTO By Format"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Format",
            "Load path",
            "Speed"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "RDB",
              "binary parse",
              "seconds per GB"
            ],
            [
              "Hybrid AOF",
              "RDB base + tail",
              "close behind"
            ],
            [
              "Plain AOF",
              "re-dispatch every command",
              "slowest by far"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--fix` cuts at the bad point — everything after is gone",
            "There is no partial RDB load, ever"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Restart & Recovery Behaviour (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Damaged Files"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Damage",
            "Redis does",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Bad RDB checksum",
              "refuses to start",
              "older backup"
            ],
            [
              "Truncated AOF tail",
              "loads, warns",
              "nothing"
            ],
            [
              "Corrupt AOF middle",
              "exits",
              "`redis-check-aof --fix`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stopping Cleanly"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`SHUTDOWN` does a final blocking save if saves exist",
            "`SHUTDOWN NOSAVE` skips it; `kill -9` always skips",
            "Redis 7 waits for lagging replicas, `shutdown-timeout 10`",
            "`DEBUG RELOAD` saves and reloads in place — a round-trip test"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Restore Drill",
          "items": [
            "Stop Redis first",
            "Drop the file into `dir`, right name and owner",
            "Start Redis — it loads on boot",
            "Never copy into a running instance's `dir`"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "RDB vs AOF: Side by Side",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Loss, Size, Speed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "RDB",
            "AOF"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Loss window",
              "minutes",
              "~1s / ~1 cmd"
            ],
            [
              "File size",
              "compact binary",
              "much larger"
            ],
            [
              "Restart",
              "fastest",
              "slowest (plain)"
            ],
            [
              "Overhead",
              "fork spike only",
              "per-write + fsync"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hybrid AOF sits between on both size and load speed",
            "RDB costs nothing at all between snapshots",
            "AOF pays a small constant cost on every write"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Operating Them"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Axis",
            "RDB",
            "AOF"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Backup",
              "one `cp`-able file",
              "dir + manifest"
            ],
            [
              "Point-in-time",
              "hourly restore points",
              "as of the crash"
            ],
            [
              "Disk I/O",
              "periodic burst",
              "steady append"
            ],
            [
              "Blast radius",
              "unusable wholesale",
              "truncate, salvage"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Backups Still Need RDB",
          "text": "AOF gives you \"now\". Only archived snapshots give you \"yesterday at 3pm\" — which is what a bad `FLUSHALL` needs."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Host Crash Ranking"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "nothing",
              "RDB",
              "AOF everysec",
              "AOF always"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Left to right: weakest to strongest on one box",
            "AOF `always` is the ceiling for a single node",
            "Both mechanisms fork, so neither escapes COW",
            "Both show up in `latest_fork_usec`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Choosing"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pick",
            "When"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Both",
              "production; Redis's own advice"
            ],
            [
              "RDB only",
              "cache-like data, huge set, fast restart"
            ],
            [
              "AOF only",
              "disk cheap, low loss, no file backups"
            ],
            [
              "Neither",
              "pure cache, warmup is cheap"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "AOF-only is rare — you still want RDB backups",
            "RDB is the DR artifact, AOF is the low-RPO log",
            "\"Neither\" assumes a real system of record behind it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "One sentence: which do I run?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Both — `appendonly yes` plus `save` lines",
            "AOF covers the last second, RDB the last week",
            "You pay the fork tax either way"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Gotchas & Common Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "MISCONF Locks Writes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "MISCONF Redis is configured to save RDB snapshots,",
            "but is currently not able to persist on disk.",
            "# usually a full disk or bad `dir` permissions"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Writes are rejected because a BGSAVE failed",
            "Fix the disk, not `stop-writes-on-bgsave-error no`",
            "That flag turns loud failure into silent data loss"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Disk Space Arithmetic"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A BGSAVE writes a full temp copy before renaming",
            "An AOF rewrite writes a full new base too",
            "Each needs room for a second whole dataset",
            "Sizing `dir` at 1x is how you meet MISCONF"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Config Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mistake",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`appendonly yes` in file, no AOF",
              "boots empty"
            ],
            [
              "`CONFIG SET`, no `CONFIG REWRITE`",
              "reverts on restart"
            ],
            [
              "`SAVE` on a big instance",
              "blocks for minutes"
            ],
            [
              "`no-appendfsync-on-rewrite yes`",
              "unmonitored footgun"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`SAVE` exists for scripts and shutdown paths, not you",
            "The rewrite window is exactly when durability quietly drops"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Kernel Bites"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "Can't save in background: fork: Cannot allocate memory",
            "# missing vm.overcommit_memory=1, intermittent under load",
            "# THP left on: mystery multi-hundred-ms spikes at save time"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Copying Files Safely",
          "items": [
            "Copying `dump.rdb` mid-BGSAVE is safe — rename saves you",
            "Copying the temp file is not — it is half written",
            "ext4 `data=writeback` is weaker than `data=ordered`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Replica Assumptions"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Snapshots on a primary hurt latency — move them to a replica",
            "But that replica's dataset can lag the primary",
            "A replica does not persist its own view unless configured",
            "Never assume the replica has a usable RDB"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Gotchas & Common Mistakes (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "FLUSHALL Is A Race",
          "text": "It replicates and it lands in the AOF. Recovery means grabbing a pre-incident RDB fast, before a rewrite overwrites the history."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Untested Backups Aren't Backups",
          "items": [
            "Restore into a scratch instance on a schedule",
            "Diff `DBSIZE` against the source",
            "Spot-check a handful of known keys"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Production Playbook & Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Baseline Config",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "conf",
          "lines": [
            "appendonly yes",
            "appendfsync everysec",
            "aof-use-rdb-preamble yes",
            "save 900 1",
            "save 300 100"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Keep `stop-writes-on-bgsave-error yes` — fail loudly",
            "`dir` on a dedicated volume, 2-3x dataset headroom",
            "Owned by the `redis` user, not root"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Host Prep",
          "items": [
            "THP set to `never`",
            "`vm.overcommit_memory=1`",
            "`maxmemory` well below RAM for COW headroom"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Monitor These Five"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Metric",
            "Alert when"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`rdb_last_bgsave_status`",
              "not `ok`"
            ],
            [
              "`aof_last_bgrewrite_status`",
              "not `ok`"
            ],
            [
              "`aof_last_write_status`",
              "not `ok`"
            ],
            [
              "`latest_fork_usec`",
              "over latency budget"
            ],
            [
              "`rdb_last_save_time`",
              "older than your RPO"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`rdb_changes_since_last_save` is the sixth to watch",
            "It tells you what a crash would cost right now"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Backup Pipeline"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "BGSAVE on replica",
              "LASTSAVE advances",
              "redis-check-rdb",
              "ship offsite, timestamped"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Production Playbook & Recap (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Retention",
          "items": [
            "Hourly for a day",
            "Daily for a month",
            "Enough to undo a logical mistake found late"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Durability Ladder"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "none",
              "RDB",
              "AOF everysec",
              "AOF always",
              "+ WAITAOF"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pay `always` where you must, not globally",
            "`WAITAOF 1 1 <timeout>` on critical writes instead",
            "Redis is a fast tier, never the last copy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Whole Handbook",
          "text": "Fork and COW are the shared tax; `write()` vs `fsync()` is the shared distinction. Test your restore before you need it."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Lines To Keep"
        },
        {
