  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of REDIS PERSISTENCE. Your Redis just restarted — how much did you lose? The honest answer is a config line, not a feeling: RDB gives you a forked point-in-time snapshot and minutes of loss, AOF gives you a command log with an fsync dial, and hybrid gives you most of both. 10 pages on snapshots, copy-on-write cost, the everysec-is-really-2s footnote, the AOF-beats-RDB load trap that boots an empty dataset, and the production config to just copy.",
